<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout>
    <title>Section 1.2 - Row Operations</title>

    <page>
        <p>
            <term>Linear systems:</term> <md/>
            <md>
                \begin{alignedat}{4}
    x \amp  {}+{}  \amp 2y \amp \amp \amp {}={}  \amp 4 \\
     \amp    \amp -3y \amp {}-{} \amp 3z \amp {}={}  \amp 3 \\
    -3x \amp  {}-{}  \amp 2y \amp {}+{} \amp z \amp {}={}  \amp -10 \\
  \end{alignedat}
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                \begin{alignedat}{4}
    x \amp  {}+{}  \amp 2y \amp \amp \amp {}={}  \amp 4 \\
     \amp    \amp -3y \amp {}-{} \amp 3z \amp {}={}  \amp 3 \\
     \amp   \amp 4y \amp {}+{} \amp z \amp {}={}  \amp 2 \\
  \end{alignedat}
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                \begin{alignedat}{4}
    x \amp  {}+{}  \amp 2y \amp \amp \amp {}={}  \amp 4 \\
     \amp    \amp y \amp {}+{} \amp z \amp {}={}  \amp -1 \\
     \amp   \amp 4y \amp {}+{} \amp z \amp {}={}  \amp 2 \\
  \end{alignedat}
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                \begin{alignedat}{4}
    x \amp  {}+{}  \amp 2y \amp \amp \amp {}={}  \amp 4 \\
     \amp    \amp y \amp {}+{} \amp z \amp {}={}  \amp -1 \\
     \amp   \amp  \amp  \amp -3z \amp {}={}  \amp 6 \\
  \end{alignedat}
            </md>

                        <md/> <md/>

            <md>
                \begin{alignedat}{4}
    x \amp  {}+{}  \amp 2y \amp \amp \amp {}={}  \amp 4 \\
     \amp    \amp y \amp {}+{} \amp z \amp {}={}  \amp -1 \\
     \amp   \amp  \amp  \amp z \amp {}={}  \amp -2 \\
  \end{alignedat}
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                \begin{alignedat}{4}
    x \amp  {}+{}  \amp 2y \amp  {}={}  \amp 4 \\
     \amp    \amp     y \amp {}={}  \amp 1 \\
     \amp   \amp   z \amp {}={}  \amp -2 \\
  \end{alignedat}
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                \begin{alignedat}{4}
     \amp x \amp  {}={}  \amp 2 \\
    \amp     y \amp {}={}  \amp 1 \\
      \amp   z \amp {}={}  \amp -2 \\
  \end{alignedat}
            </md>
        </p>
    </page>

    <page>
        <p workspace="1in">
            <term>Row operations:</term> <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                R_3 + 3R_1 \rightarrow R_3
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                -\frac{1}{3}R_2 \rightarrow R_2
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                R_3 + (-4)R_2 \rightarrow R_3
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                -\frac{1}{3}R_3 \rightarrow R_3
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                R_2 + (-1)R_3 \rightarrow R_2
            </md>
            <md/> <md/>
            <md>
                R_1 + (-2)R_2 \rightarrow R_1
            </md>
            <md/> <md/> <md/> <md/>
        </p>

        <paragraphs>
            <title>Instructions</title>

            <p>
                <ol>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            You are given 7 systems of linear equations.
                            Put the linear systems in order from most
                            complicated to least complicated.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Then, ask your for the next set.
                            You'll get 6 row operatons.
                            Identify which row operation takes you from one
                            system to the next in your list.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            What you just did was unscramble the steps of
                            Gaussian Elimination!
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </p>
        </paragraphs>
    </page>
</handout>